 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   Sparse regions: If SfM points are sparse, voxel coverage may be incomplete. [G] Ensure voxel grid covers the entire scene bounding box, even if voxels are empty initially.
-*   Precision: Interpolation weights must be normalized.
+- Interpolation artifacts near voxel boundaries may cause discontinuities in predicted attributes [G].
+- Sparse SfM regions may lack sufficient voxel coverage, requiring integration modules like DART/AGE for proper seeding [S1].
 
